{
  "name": "golden-004-contracts-gate-and-fsrs-scheduling",
  "description": "WP-06's closed loop, end to end: one captured target, three contracts on the same KnowledgeComponent, and every branch of the evidence gate exercised against them. Reviews before promotion and while merely kept reach nothing (T-02); a reveal-before-recall review submitted as `good` is scheduled as `again` (T-06); the lookup and the tier-D exposure of the same component are recorded and refused (T-07, T-08); an unconfirmed `easy` is refused and the confirmed one is not (REQ-DM-07); the production contract is inert under `learn` and live under `master` (REQ-DM-09). Meaning, reading, and production carry three separate memory states, so no grade on one moves another (T-05). Because every interval below comes from pinned ts-fsrs 5.4.1 (FSRS-6) at desired retention 0.90, this fixture is also the replay gate on FSRS determinism (T-03, REQ-SCH-01).",
